  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "A rank four Gu Master’s secretly built strength inheritance on Bai Gu Mountain is named as belonging to the righteous path.",
      "chapters": [
        43
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "sys_gu_master",
        "loc_bai_gu_mountain"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Crowd praise can call a rank four Gu Master who refuses to bully the weaker party a role model of the righteous path.",
      "chapters": [
        45
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "Shang clan sits among the leaders of the Southern Border righteous paths, yet Shang clan city still takes demonic path goods and leaves room for freedom of trade.",
      "chapters": [
        229
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "southern-border-example",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "fac_shang_clan",
        "reg_southern_border",
        "loc_shang_clan_city"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "People raised under clan life carry righteous path ideology as habit, and notice when others show demonic nature.",
      "chapters": [
        253
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "southern-border-example",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "Shang clan itself is called a righteous path overlord.",
      "chapters": [
        271
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "southern-border-example",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "Righteous Gu Masters rely on clans, clansmen help, and safely obtained resources. That backing gives a sense of security and trust among them. Wei Yang, who converted from demonic to righteous, frames the contrast this way: the righteous faction flourishes while the demonic faction is suppressed, because lone demonic Gu Masters lack that support and turn on each other.",
      "chapters": [
        280
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "clan-backing",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_wei_yang",
        "sys_demonic_path"
      ]
    }
  ],
